 @EdoTensai947  If you would take a look at gpu charts, you would see how well the graphics cards perform compared to others. 
You'd have to go with the RTX 3070 if you want to overtake the RX 6700 XT, but then you might as well consider switching to the RX 6800. In the end, it all depends on what your needs are, what you want to do with it, and what is the cheapest graphics card for your needs.

For example, the RX 6700 XT is a good 1440p card, while the RX 6600 or RX 6600 XT is a good 1080p card.

